# The build context is sent to the daemon before the Dockerfile runs, and line 6
# of the Dockerfile is `COPY . .` — which lands *after* `RUN npm ci`. Without
# this file the host's node_modules is copied over the freshly installed Linux
# one, so the build compiles against whatever TypeScript the developer happens to
# have locally. On a machine carrying node_modules from an older project that
# meant TypeScript 4.x, and tsconfig.json's "moduleResolution": "bundler" and
# "allowImportingTsExtensions" failed as unknown options even though the lockfile
# pins 5.9.3. It also sent 731 MB of context instead of a few hundred KB.
node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
*.log
.eslintcache
